From: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: fix spurious MDIO timeout using
 read_poll_timeout

Port of MediaTek vendor patch 999-eth-53 (mtk-openwrt-feeds,
25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12), plus one addition not
in the vendor diff: this tree does not otherwise pull in
<linux/iopoll.h>, so read_poll_timeout() is undefined without an
explicit include - added it rather than relying on an implicit
transitive include. Inserted at the tail of the existing include
block (after <net/page_pool/helpers.h>) rather than right after
<linux/of_net.h> like the vendor's own patch: several already-applied
local/backport patches (not just 999-qos-01) insert additional
headers immediately after of_net.h by the time this patch's turn in
the series comes up, and the tail of the block is the one anchor
confirmed stable across every currently-applied local patch.

The current mtk_mdio_busy_wait() implementation has a race window
between the PHY_IAC_ACCESS check and the subsequent time_after() check.
If the CPU is preempted during this window and the PHY completes its
operation, the function may incorrectly report a timeout even though the
hardware succeeded.

Fix this by replacing with read_poll_timeout(), which performs a final
hardware register read before declaring a timeout.

No chip-version gate - applies to this tree's NETSYSv1 baseline as-is.
This board's MT7531 switch is driven over exactly this internal MDIO
bus. See docs/e8450-mtk-feeds-audit-2026-09.md S2.

Signed-off-by: MediaTek vendor feed <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -33,5 +33,6 @@
 #include <net/gso.h>
 #include <net/checksum.h>
 #include <net/page_pool/helpers.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
 
 #include "mtk_eth_soc.h"
@@ -325,18 +326,19 @@ static u32 mtk_r32(struct mtk_eth *eth,
 
 static int mtk_mdio_busy_wait(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 {
-	unsigned long t_start = jiffies;
+	u32 val;
+	int ret;
 
-	while (1) {
-		if (!(mtk_r32(eth, MTK_PHY_IAC) & PHY_IAC_ACCESS))
-			return 0;
-		if (time_after(jiffies, t_start + PHY_IAC_TIMEOUT))
-			break;
-		cond_resched();
-	}
+	ret = read_poll_timeout(mtk_r32, val,
+				!(val & PHY_IAC_ACCESS),
+				10,
+				jiffies_to_usecs(PHY_IAC_TIMEOUT),
+				false,
+				eth, MTK_PHY_IAC);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(eth->dev, "mdio: MDIO timeout\n");
 
-	dev_err(eth->dev, "mdio: MDIO timeout\n");
-	return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int _mtk_mdio_write_c22(struct mtk_eth *eth, u32 phy_addr, u32 phy_reg,
